# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.local

# Logs
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Saved projects are the user's own work, not part of the repo.
# The folder itself stays tracked (see projects/.gitkeep) so the app has somewhere to write.
projects/*.smproj.json
projects/*.tmp

# Goldman Sans is Goldman Sachs' corporate typeface, licensed under their own
# terms — not an open font license like the four self-hosted families in
# public/fonts/. Redistributing it from a public repo is a licensing decision,
# so it is untracked by default. The files stay on disk and work locally; a
# fresh clone falls back to Inter via the CSS font stack.
# Remove these two lines only if you have confirmed you may redistribute it.
public/fonts/goldman/
# Anchored with a leading slash, and this is not cosmetic: macOS sets core.ignorecase=true,
# so an unanchored `Fonts/` also matched `public/fonts/` and silently excluded every
# self-hosted family — the whole point of not using a CDN — from the repository.
/Fonts/

# Fonts installed through the in-app browser, and any font files you dropped in yourself.
# Untracked, for the same reason as Goldman Sans above plus two of its own:
#
#   1. Licensing. Google Fonts families are overwhelmingly OFL and would be fine to
#      redistribute — but this directory is not Google-only. Uploaded files land here too,
#      and those are licensed however you licensed them. The directory is unknown-provenance
#      by construction, so it does not go in a public repo by default.
#   2. They are a cache, not source. Every family here is one click away from being
#      re-downloaded, and each one is a few hundred KB of binary that will never diff.
#   3. Which families you installed is your taste, not the project's configuration.
#
# installed.css is generated from whatever is actually on disk every time the dev server
# starts, so a fresh clone is immediately consistent — it just declares nothing until you
# install something. The four families in public/fonts/webfonts.css stay tracked and are
# what the app falls back to.
#
# Committing a family deliberately: confirm its LICENSE.txt permits redistribution, then
# `git add -f public/fonts/installed/<family-slug>`.
public/fonts/installed/*
!public/fonts/installed/.gitkeep

# The drop folder — font files you put in public/fonts/custom/ yourself. Untracked for the same
# reasons as public/fonts/installed/ above: they are your own files of unknown provenance and
# licensing, they are binary that will never diff meaningfully, and which fonts you keep here is
# your taste rather than the project's configuration. custom.css is GENERATED from whatever is on
# disk every time the dev server starts, so it is ignored too — a fresh clone regenerates it (and
# it just declares nothing until you drop a font in). The folder itself stays tracked via .gitkeep
# so the app always has somewhere to scan, and README.md stays tracked so the instructions travel.
#
# Committing a font deliberately: confirm its licence permits redistribution, then
# `git add -f "public/fonts/custom/<family>"`.
public/fonts/custom/*
!public/fonts/custom/.gitkeep
!public/fonts/custom/README.md

# Local Claude Code / assistant config (not part of the product)
.claude/
